<item><title>Congo holds aquaculture forum as local fish output falls short of demand</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-holds-aquaculture-forum-as-local-fish-output-falls-61a42a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-holds-aquaculture-forum-as-local-fish-output-falls-61a42a/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>The country needs about 163 000 tonnes of fish a year, while local production reaches nearly 60 000 tonnes, leaving a gap of more than 100 000 tonnes.</description><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:05:29 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-holds-aquaculture-forum-as-local-fish-output-falls-61a42a/share.jpg" length="45909" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-holds-aquaculture-forum-as-local-fish-output-falls-61a42a/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
